			"notes": "With this update, some features has been added/changed:\n\n## Features\n- Some new advancements have been added: \"Lighten Up\", \"Minecraft: Trial(s) Edition\", \"It Spreads\"\n- Copper Bulbs can now be scraped with an axe to make them brighter (gives advancement \"Lighten Up\")\n- Most copper blocks can now be scraped\n- Most copper blocks will now oxidize over time\n- Most copper blocks can now be waxed to stop oxidizing\n- New particles appear when a copper block is being waxed\n- New sounds have been added\n- All tuff variants have been added (walls/slabs/stairs/chiseled/bricks)\n- Coral blocks are now available in creative mode (currently no function)\n- Blast furnace with GUI (BETA: There are still a few bugs!!)\n- Added a bell like in new versions (currently no sound, but it already looks like the original)\n\n## Changes\n- Missing translations have been added: pottery sherds, blackstone slab, copper torch, jungle button\n- Copper Bulbs are now working like in new versions (redstone impulse to activate/deactivate them)\n- The UBM Edition text on start screen has been rescaled to make it less pixelated\n- Now, diamond tools can also be shift-clicked into the smithing table\n\n## Bugs fixed\n- Bamboo rafts now have the right model\n- Bamboo rafts are now spawned using the correct item\n- Armor trims could not be applied to armor\n- It was possible to upgrade diamond armor without using the upgrade trim or netherite ingot\n- Glitched copies of wall items in creative inventory have been removed (Thanks to @EggmanEmpire for reporting!)\n- Crafting of netherite is finally like in new versions (Thanks to @Switch-Back18 for reporting!)\n\n## Upcoming with Pre-Release 3\nThe new version 1.3.0 will introduce a config file for activating/deactivating features and to control e.g. the health or damage of several entities added by this mod. \n**A first version of the config is already in this release, but won't be used by the mod.** These funtions will be enrolled with next beta versions.\n\n\nThanks to everyone for reporting issues and giving suggestions on the mod! I really appreciate that and I try my best to continue the development of this amazing project. Thank you! ♥"
		},
